            <ArticleTitle>Use of 99mTc-sestamibi Single-photon Emission Computed Tomography / X-ray Computed Tomography in the Diagnosis of Hybrid Oncocytic / Chromophobe Tumor in a Pediatric Patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0090-4295(17)31212-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.urology.2017.11.015</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The differential diagnosis of solid renal neoplasms in adolescence includes aggressive malignancy and indolent oncocytic tumors, which are typically indistinguishable using conventional imaging. We report the use of 99mTc-sestamibi single-photon emission computed tomography / x-ray computed tomography (SPECT/CT) in characterizing enhancing renal neoplasms in a pediatric patient. Genetic testing suggested a hereditary syndrome associated with aggressive malignancy, whereas renal mass biopsy suggested an oncocytic tumor. 99mTc-sestamibi SPECT/CT indicated probable oncocytomas or hybrid oncocytic / chomophobe tumors. Enucleative resection was performed with final pathology demonstrating hybrid oncocytic / chomophobe tumors. This case highlights the potential utility of 99mTc-sestamibi SPECT/CT in characterizing indeterminate enhancing renal neoplasm in pediatric patients.</AbstractText>
